/target
# This workspace overrides CARGO_TARGET_DIR to a shared location outside the
# repo (see .cargo/config.toml comments + the dev-machine env var), so any
# `target/` directory found IN-TREE (e.g. `crates/region/target/`) is never
# real cargo build output — it's a tool writing a relative "target/..." path
# from the crate's own CWD. First seen from captrack's `autodump` feature
# (writes `target/captrack-pgo/profile-*.json` on process exit unless
# CAPTRACK_DUMP_DIR is set), task #656. Any crate under crates/ could exhibit
# this once captrack is added as a dev-dependency there too.
**/target/
/.crush
/.idea
/tmp
# R6-OPT-A6: per-run raw provenance dumps from scripts/paired-ab-runner.mjs --
# generated output, accumulates one timestamped JSON per invocation, not source.
# SAME scratch-by-default / `git add -f`-when-cited policy as `_raw_*.log`
# below: some reports (R31_10 §5.2, R32-0/c72a27b, R32-12/e88390b) force-add
# specific paired_ab_runs JSON filenames as their cited provenance, and 33 such
# files remain tracked across rounds 14-32. R33-5 (task #510) deliberately chose
# the curated `_raw_*.log` route instead (truncatable per R14-10, reproducible)
# -- both are legitimate citation homes; this bare ignore line previously
# lacked the exception clause `_raw_*.log` already documents (R34-1/task #520).
/docs/perf/paired_ab_runs/
# R13-10 (task #280): scratch raw command-output logs from bench/test/iai
# sweeps (`docs/perf/_raw_*.log`) are throwaway by default -- ignored so ad-hoc
# local runs never accumulate as untracked noise (22 such files had piled up
# across R9-R11 before this rule). EXCEPTION: when a perf-gate report in
# docs/perf/*.md cites specific `_raw_*.log` filenames as its evidence (the
# R13-6/R13-8/R13-9 gate docs already do this), `git add -f` those specific
# files so the cited evidence is reproducible from the commit, not just from
# a re-run. Do not `git add -f` logs a doc does not name.
/docs/perf/_raw_*.log
# task #493: scripts/capture-measurement-identity.mjs --patch-hash now saves
# the patch it hashes to docs/perf/_raw_identity_<tree-sha-prefix>.patch --
# same "scratch by default, git add -f only when a report cites it" policy
# as the _raw_*.log rule immediately above.
/docs/perf/_raw_identity_*.patch
# R34-7 (task #526): per-run raw provenance JSONs from
# scripts/r34_7_causal_harness.mjs — same scratch-by-default policy as
# paired_ab_runs above.
/docs/perf/r34_7_runs/
# task #551 (R34-review F7): per-run raw provenance JSONs from
# scripts/r34_23_realloc_direct_harness.mjs / r34_23_vec_harness.mjs — same
# scratch-by-default policy as paired_ab_runs / r34_7_runs above. This rule
# was missing when `ba716a0` (R34-23/task #542) first created the directory,
# which let its 258 KiB direct_raw.json land as an ordinary tracked file
# instead of through the deliberate git-add-f-when-cited gate (see
# docs/perf/OPEN_ITEMS.md for the tracked deviation record). Already-tracked
# files in this directory stay tracked despite the ignore rule (git does not
# untrack on a later .gitignore addition) — this only prevents FUTURE files
# in the directory from being added without a deliberate `git add -f`.
/docs/perf/r34_23_runs/
# L6 (task #619, N6 of docs/reviews/2026-08-05-fh-release-readiness-verification-review.md):
# .claude/ holds local tool state (scheduled_tasks.json, settings.json —
# the latter contains this machine's local paths, see N5) — not project
# source, never meant to be tracked. Untracked .claude/ was also blocking
# `cargo package` from running without --allow-dirty during release-gap
# verification this session.
/.claude/
